{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"631ffcc2def23959","name":"card_unit_lovat_scouts","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_lovat_scouts","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LOVAT SCOUTS","text":"Your cards have the Navy type while on top of your deck.","flavorText":"The Lovat Scouts, originally a Scottish Highland regiment, was a unit which served with the British Army from 1900 to 1969. They were the first military unit known to wear a ghillie suit and were recognized for their advanced reconnaissance skills. In 1916, the Lovat Scouts became the British Army’s first official sniper unit, called \"sharpshooters.\" The regiment served in many conflicts, including WWI and WWII. During the early stages of WWII they were stationed in the Faroe Islands, guarding against a German invasion. In December 1943, the regiment was sent to Canada for specialist ski and mountain training in Jasper National Park, focusing on cross-country movement, survival in cold climates, and mountain ascents. After completing their training and returning to the UK, the Scouts deployed to Italy in July 1944. There, they participated in the later stages of the Italian campaign until the German surrender in May 1945. Following the war, the Lovat Scouts advanced through the Brenner Pass into Austria and Bavaria to locate senior Nazi and SS personnel.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_lovat_scouts","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_lovat_scouts_title","SourceString":"LOVAT SCOUTS","LocalizedString":"LOVAT SCOUTS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_lovat_scouts_text","SourceString":"Your cards have the Navy type while on top of your deck.","LocalizedString":"Your cards have the Navy type while on top of your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_lovat_scouts_history","SourceString":"The Lovat Scouts, originally a Scottish Highland regiment, was a unit which served with the British Army from 1900 to 1969. They were the first military unit known to wear a ghillie suit and were recognized for their advanced reconnaissance skills. In 1916, the Lovat Scouts became the British Army’s first official sniper unit, called \"sharpshooters.\" The regiment served in many conflicts, including WWI and WWII. During the early stages of WWII they were stationed in the Faroe Islands, guarding against a German invasion. In December 1943, the regiment was sent to Canada for specialist ski and mountain training in Jasper National Park, focusing on cross-country movement, survival in cold climates, and mountain ascents. After completing their training and returning to the UK, the Scouts deployed to Italy in July 1944. There, they participated in the later stages of the Italian campaign until the German surrender in May 1945. Following the war, the Lovat Scouts advanced through the Brenner Pass into Austria and Bavaria to locate senior Nazi and SS personnel.","LocalizedString":"The Lovat Scouts, originally a Scottish Highland regiment, was a unit which served with the British Army from 1900 to 1969. They were the first military unit known to wear a ghillie suit and were recognized for their advanced reconnaissance skills. In 1916, the Lovat Scouts became the British Army’s first official sniper unit, called \"sharpshooters.\" The regiment served in many conflicts, including WWI and WWII. During the early stages of WWII they were stationed in the Faroe Islands, guarding against a German invasion. In December 1943, the regiment was sent to Canada for specialist ski and mountain training in Jasper National Park, focusing on cross-country movement, survival in cold climates, and mountain ascents. After completing their training and returning to the UK, the Scouts deployed to Italy in July 1944. There, they participated in the later stages of the Italian campaign until the German surrender in May 1945. Following the war, the Lovat Scouts advanced through the Brenner Pass into Austria and Bavaria to locate senior Nazi and SS personnel."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLocationMoved","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterDeckChanged"],"cipher":2,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/NavalWarfare/t_lovat_scouts.t_lovat_scouts","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/LOVAT_SCOUTS.LOVAT_SCOUTS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":342.0,"Y":512.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_lovat_scouts_photo","SourceString":"Men of Lovat Scouts in ghillie suits. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"Men of Lovat Scouts in ghillie suits. Date unknown."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"","Key":"0DBC5F184A8F0CFAA1A9D6BB449E2AC6","SourceString":"Infantry","LocalizedString":"Infantry"},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryS'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryS.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeLight_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeLight.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"threat_level":0.1},"variables":[{"name":"affectedCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_lovat_scouts","owner":"card_unit_lovat_scouts_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":